  "graph_implications": [
    "The initial error list contains both test/emulator modules and non-test consumers such as netbpfload and secretkeeper defaults; this review does not assume that every failing consumer is a test.",
    "Soong parses a source graph larger than the final recovery image. Missing shared defaults in otherwise unneeded roots can stop graph generation before link/install reachability is established.",
    "Supported PRODUCT_SOURCE_ROOT_DIRS selection is preferable for the initial no-network/no-crypto target only when its implementation still rejects missing dependencies consumed by retained modules. The separate build audit owns verification of that behavior.",
    "If a retained module requires one of these defaults, restore the correct r1 provider with its true flags/dependencies and applicable metadata. Do not invent empty defaults, disable missing-dependency checks, or copy definitions from Evolution bka.",
    "Restoring all five full source roots adds substantial unrelated test, emulator, VM and NN graph surface. The reference checkouts contain 506 Android.bp files and are not a measured r1 graph or download-size estimate.",
    "Selecting just one Android.bp is not necessarily sufficient: it can contain additional modules, inherit parent licenses/defaults, or refer to headers, aconfig inputs and Rust proc macros.",
    "No speculative full AOSP restoration is recommended. A complete strict recovery graph remains the required validation."
  ],
